Strip the quotes CMake writes into object response files before nvcc_wrapper word-splits them.
CMake 3.29 and later put the object list of a large link into CMakeFiles/<target>.dir/objects*.rsp
with quoted paths. nvcc_wrapper reads the file into its own argument list, and because every path
then starts with a quote none of them match the wrapper's object patterns; they are glued into one
-Xcompiler argument, which exceeds the single-argument limit of the kernel (128 KiB) when liblammps
links its three 128 KiB object lists, and nvcc fails with "Argument list too long" (exit 126).
Kokkos 5.2.1 as bundled with LAMMPS 30Sep2026 has the problem; kokkos/kokkos#9573 (merged
2026-10-01) is the upstream fix.
--- lammps-stable_30Sep2026.orig/lib/kokkos/bin/nvcc_wrapper
+++ lammps-stable_30Sep2026/lib/kokkos/bin/nvcc_wrapper
@@ -494,7 +494,13 @@ do
   @*.rsp)
     rsp_file="${1#@}"
     # Need $1 at the start so it gets shifted out instead of the first thing in the rsp file
-    set -- $1 $(cat "$rsp_file") "${@:2}"
+    # Strip quotes from tokens: CMake >=3.29 writes quoted paths into objects1.rsp, so unquoted word-splitting mis-handles them as -Xcompiler args
+    # Known issues:
+    #   1) Escaped quotes will corrupt the response file.
+    #   Pre-Existing:
+    #      2) Objects that end in .a/.so/.dylib (e.g: --option=value.a) are mis-classified (with stipped quotes: link arg, without: -Xcompiler arg)
+    #      3) Quoted whitespace is lost: paths containing spaces are still split
+    set -- $1 $(sed 's/"//g' "$rsp_file") "${@:2}"
     ;;
   #Handle object files which always need to use "-Xlinker": -x cu applies to all input files, so give them to linker, except if only linking
   @*|*.dylib)
